Move LaunchedEffect into the composable, with `LaunchedEffect(screen, parentStatus?)`. Simpler: inside Surface, after when, add:

```kotlin
val guardState by engine.state.collectAsState()
LaunchedEffect(screen, guardState) {
   if (screen != PARENT) return@LaunchedEffect
   while (isActive) { ... }
}
```
But that effect needs to be in a composable. Put in setContent:

```kotlin
setContent {
  MaterialTheme... {
    Surface {
      val guardState by engine.state.collectAsState()
      if (screen == PARENT) ParentPoller(guardState) ... 
```

Simplest: define a composable `ParentUnlockEffect(engine, watchRepository, screen, onAdopt, onStatus)`? State mutation from coroutine inside composable okay (screen var is activity field).

Let me restructure: keep LaunchedEffect at top of Surface content:

```kotlin
setContent {
  MaterialTheme(...) {
    Surface(Modifier.fillMaxSize()) {
      val guardState by engine.state.collectAsState()
      LaunchedEffect(screen, guardState) {
         if (screen != PARENT) return@LaunchedEffect
         if (guardState == GRANTED || WATCHING || IDLE) { finish(); return@... }
         while (isActive) {
            val grant = ...
            ...
            delay(5000)
         }
      }
      when(screen) {...}
    }
  }
}
```

Careful: recomposition on parentStatus changes won't restart effect (keys only screen, guardState). Good. But when engine state changes to GRANTED, effect restarts and finishes. Also check state at loop start.

Need import collectAsState and getValue already imported. Add `androidx.compose.runtime.collectAsState`.

Remove the old LaunchedEffect block after setContent.

Implement.

